        "answerKey": "1. Let F(x, y, z) = x^3 + y^3 + z^3 - 3xyz - 4 = 0.\n2. Evaluate at (1, 1, 2): F(1, 1, 2) = 1 + 1 + 8 - 6 - 4 = 0. Point satisfies the equation.\n3. Compute partial derivative w.r.t z:\n   \\partial F/\\partial z = 3z^2 - 3xy.\n   Evaluate at (1, 1, 2): 3(2)^2 - 3(1)(1) = 12 - 3 = 9 != 0.\n4. Since \\partial F/\\partial z != 0, the Implicit Function Theorem guarantees that z = g(x,y) is defined implicitly in a neighborhood.\n5. Find \\partial z/\\partial x using formula:\n   \\partial z/\\partial x = -(\\partial F/\\partial x) / (\\partial F/\\partial z).\n   \\partial F/\\partial x = 3x^2 - 3yz. At (1,1,2): 3(1)^2 - 3(1)(2) = 3 - 6 = -3.\n   Thus, \\partial z/\\partial x = -(-3) / 9 = 3/9 = 1/3."
