        "answerKey": "1. Write $\\mathbf{A} = A_x\\hat{i}+A_y\\hat{j}+A_z\\hat{k}$. Compute $\\mathbf{B} = \\nabla\\times\\mathbf{A}$: $B_x = \\partial_y A_z - \\partial_z A_y$, etc.\n2. Compute $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{B}$: x-component = $\\partial_y B_z - \\partial_z B_y$.\n3. Substituting and expanding: $= \\partial_y(\\partial_x A_y - \\partial_y A_x) - \\partial_z(\\partial_z A_x - \\partial_x A_z) = \\partial_x(\\partial_y A_y + \\partial_z A_z) - (\\partial_{yy}+\\partial_{zz})A_x$.\n4. Adding and subtracting $\\partial_{xx}A_x$: $= \\partial_x(\\partial_x A_x + \\partial_y A_y + \\partial_z A_z) - (\\partial_{xx}+\\partial_{yy}+\\partial_{zz})A_x = [\\nabla(\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf{A})]_x - [\\nabla^2\\mathbf{A}]_x$.\n5. By symmetry, same for y and z components. Hence proved."
